How about this scenario:

You just finished cleaning up all the nasties on the last level, killed
the High Priest(ess) of Moloch, and have the Amulet of Yendor.  You offer
the Amulet to Moloch on his altar and are rewarded with the honor of 
becoming Moloch's new High Priest(ess) and guarding the Amulet from all
future adventurers.

The game would end for you at this point, but your character would live on
in a permanent bones file that everyone on your system would have to clear.
You would have the use of all of your stuff, spells, and pets too!  But for
this immortality you would give up your shot at the high score list, except
as the cause of death for other hapless adventurers.

This should be easy to implement within the current game system.  Who will
dare to make it so?

JC

ps: how about an amulet of life stealing that would accomplish a similar
effect: when worn, your game ends, creating a bones level with a (now) full
amulet of life stealing.  When the next adventurer comes along and puts it
on, your character gets recreated exactly as you were when you put it on,
and proceeds to attack the adventurer.  The amulet would then crumble to
dust.  It could be indistinguishable from an amulet of life saving and even
could be implemented so as to only work when you die (i.e. instead of
saving your life when you die, your life force gets sucked into the amulet,
waiting for the next adventurer to come along and put it on, somewhat like
a delayed amulet of life saving).
